  <!-- Engineering Science & Mathematical Modeling Section -->
  <div class="border-t border-hairline pt-10 mb-10">
    <div class="mb-6">
      <h3 class="text-lg sm:text-xl font-bold text-ink tracking-tight mb-1">
        {d.scienceTitle}
      </h3>
      <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-muted">
        {d.scienceSub}
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3 gap-6 text-xs text-muted leading-relaxed">
      <div class="p-5 rounded-2xl bg-surface-soft border border-hairline space-y-2">
        <h4 class="font-bold text-ink text-sm flex items-center gap-1.5">
          <span class="text-sky-600 font-mono">1.</span> ASTM C149 Thermal Hoop Stress
        </h4>
        <div class="p-2.5 rounded-xl bg-slate-900 text-sky-300 font-mono text-[11px] my-2">
          &sigma;_tensile = (E &middot; &alpha; &middot; &Delta;T) / (1 - &nu;) &middot; &Phi;
        </div>
        <p>
          When a cold glass container at initial temperature <code class="font-mono text-ink">T_ambient</code> enters saturated steam at <code class="font-mono text-ink">T_steam</code>, the outer surface expands rapidly while the cooler core resists expansion. This induces outer surface tensile hoop stress. Soda-lime glass has an elastic modulus <code class="font-mono text-ink">E = 72 GPa</code>, thermal expansion <code class="font-mono text-ink">&alpha; = 8.5&times;10^-6 /K</code>, and Poisson ratio <code class="font-mono text-ink">&nu; = 0.22</code>. ASTM C149 dictates a safe maximum thermal gradient <code class="font-mono text-ink">&Delta;T &le; 42&deg;C</code> to prevent fracture.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="p-5 rounded-2xl bg-surface-soft border border-hairline space-y-2">
        <h4 class="font-bold text-ink text-sm flex items-center gap-1.5">
          <span class="text-sky-600 font-mono">2.</span> Saturated Steam Condensation Flux
        </h4>
        <div class="p-2.5 rounded-xl bg-slate-900 text-sky-300 font-mono text-[11px] my-2">
          q'' = h_cond &middot; (T_steam - T_wall) &middot; [1 - e^(-t/&tau;)]
        </div>
        <p>
          Saturated steam phase change condensation yields extraordinary heat transfer coefficients (<code class="font-mono text-ink">h_cond = 6,000 to 12,000 W/m&sup2;&middot;K</code>), releasing latent heat (<code class="font-mono text-ink">h_fg = 2,257 kJ/kg</code>). This instantaneously activates shrink sleeve polymer chains (PETG, PVC, OPS) while simultaneously producing liquid condensate that must be drained and shielded via heated canopies to satisfy FDA 21 CFR &sect; 117.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="p-5 rounded-2xl bg-surface-soft border border-hairline space-y-2">
        <h4 class="font-bold text-ink text-sm flex items-center gap-1.5">
          <span class="text-sky-600 font-mono">3.</span> Stainless Pitting Resistance (PREN)
        </h4>
        <div class="p-2.5 rounded-xl bg-slate-900 text-sky-300 font-mono text-[11px] my-2">
          PREN = %Cr + 3.3&middot;(%Mo) + 16&middot;(%N)
        </div>
        <p>
          In hot moist steam tunnel plenums, acidic sanitizer residues (peracetic acid, pH 2.8) and PVC sleeve thermal degradation off-gassing (HCl) create severe chloride and acid corrosion. Grade 304 stainless steel (<code class="font-mono text-ink">PREN &asymp; 18.5</code>) suffers rapid pitting and stress corrosion cracking (CSCC). Molybdenum-stabilized 316L (<code class="font-mono text-ink">PREN &ge; 24.5</code>) resists acidic pitting liquor.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

